---
# The cluster-wide secret store every ExternalSecret references.
#
# 1Password Connect variant: Connect runs in-cluster and serves reads from a
# local encrypted cache, so no workload ever calls the 1Password cloud API.
#
# Plaintext HTTP on the in-cluster ClusterIP is deliberate: the secret-fetch
# path has to work BEFORE cert-manager and Traefik are up, and pod-to-pod
# traffic is already encrypted by the CNI between nodes. Connect's own
# NetworkPolicy is what scopes who may reach this address.
#
# Swapping backends means replacing this file, controllers/onepassword-connect/,
# and the egress patch in controllers/external-secrets/ — the ExternalSecrets
# themselves only reference ${cluster_secret_store}.
apiVersion: external-secrets.io/v1
kind: ClusterSecretStore
metadata:
  name: ${cluster_secret_store}
spec:
  # A ClusterSecretStore is cluster-scoped, so WITHOUT this block ANY namespace
  # may name it in an ExternalSecret and read EVERY item in the vault. That is
  # not a theoretical reach: a tenant namespace whose reconciliation
  # ServiceAccount holds the `admin` ClusterRole can create ExternalSecrets, so
  # an unconditioned store hands every tenant the CI runner tokens, the identity
  # provider's keys and the SMTP credentials. The store is the boundary — RBAC
  # in the tenant's own namespace cannot re-impose one.
  #
  # Access is therefore opt-in per namespace, by label. A namespace that needs
  # platform secrets carries
  #   ${cluster_node_label_domain}/cluster-secrets: "true"
  # on its Namespace object (see kubernetes/README.md, "Node label contract").
  # Namespace labels are set by manifests in THIS repository — the built-in
  # `admin` ClusterRole grants only get/list/watch on namespaces, so a tenant
  # cannot label its way in.
  #
  # A new platform module adds the label to its namespace.yaml. A TENANT must
  # not get the label: give it its own ClusterSecretStore, its own Connect token
  # and, ideally, its own vault — the pattern is in
  # kubernetes/clusters/*/tenants/README.md.
  conditions:
    - namespaceSelector:
        matchLabels:
          ${cluster_node_label_domain}/cluster-secrets: "true"
  provider:
    onepassword:
      connectHost: http://onepassword-connect.external-secrets.svc.cluster.local:8080
      vaults:
        ${cluster_secrets_vault}: 1
      auth:
        secretRef:
          connectTokenSecretRef:
            name: onepassword-connect-token
            namespace: external-secrets
            key: token
